  "title": "fix round 1 for T-1504: write the seven acceptance-named tests for B2a (predicates, claude_row_free, bounded requeue, counter reset, executed_by, pool extraction, pure snapshot)",
  "spec": "Fix round for T-1504 (goal T-1403, B2a), branch cut from task/T-1504 (commits 8f626ea, 492c538, 8ac5900 implemented executor.codex_rows / fallback_mode / claude_row_free / executed_by, the bounded claude_capacity requeue in _exhausted, Pool.row_covers / claude_has_headroom and capacity.snapshot(claude_free=)). The gate held it gate_red because NONE of the seven acceptance-named tests exist (`missing: test not defined` for every id below); the executor changed only 12 lines of tests.\n\nWrite exactly these seven tests, named exactly like this, as unittest.TestCase methods next to the existing tests in each file, using the same fixtures (tests/test_executor.py claude_pool(policy, with_codex_row) and the harness pool; tests/test_pool.py's Pool fixtures; tests/test_capacity.py's snapshot fixtures). The behaviour under test is the T-1504 spec (read bus task T-1504 for the full contract):\n1. tests/test_executor.py::test_codex_rows_and_fallback_mode_predicates: codex_rows lists only enabled execute rows with provider codex; fallback_mode(pool, now=now) is False for a Claude-only pool even with every Claude row cooling and no [codex] table, True with one enabled codex row cooling at now and on_exhausted fallback_claude, False when that row is not cooling or the policy is hold; time.time patched to raise is never called when now is given.\n2. tests/test_executor.py::test_claude_row_free_counts_free_parallelism: max_parallel - running with headroom=True; 0 when disabled, cooling at now, saturated, over daily_budget_tasks (stored counters, roll_day patched to raise), or headroom=False; headroom=None behaves like True; time.time and Pool.pick patched to raise are not called.\n3. tests/test_executor.py::test_no_codex_row_requeues_bounded_or_holds_visibly: executor.start on a Claude-only pool with pick_executor returning None and no [codex] table: (a) complexity-5 task covered by a Claude row -> queued, pipeline.hold_note 'claude_capacity', claude_capacity_until in the future, claude_capacity_requeues 1, no dispatched_at, no hold_reason, return status 'claude_capacity'; (b) uncovered complexity -> held 'no executor row covers complexity N', return status 'held'; (c) after claude_capacity_max_requeues -> held with hold_reason starting 'claude_capacity:'; held payloads have no 'pol' key; nothing raises.\n4. tests/test_executor.py::test_successful_claim_resets_claude_capacity_counters: a task carrying pipeline.claude_capacity_requeues 7 and claude_capacity_until that executor.start successfully claims (stubbed worker) has neither key afterwards.\n5. tests/test_executor.py::test_executed_by_from_row_provider: executed_by('astra','sonnet',cfg) == 'codex:astra' for a codex row id and for a bare id absent from cfg; 'claude:opus' for the claude:opus row id and for the label; 'codex:x' for 'codex:x'; 'claude:sonnet' for None with tier sonnet.\n6. tests/test_pool.py::test_row_covers_and_claude_has_headroom_extracted: Pool.row_covers matches eligible_executors' in_band decision for a paired Claude pool (split boundary inclusive on the sonnet side) and for a single row; claude_has_headroom() False when pick('execute') returns None, True otherwise.\n7. tests/test_capacity.py::test_snapshot_fallback_flag_and_pure_claude_free: Claude-only pool with every Claude row cooling -> snapshot(...)['fallback'] False and executor.fallback_mode False (patching executor.fallback_mode flips the key); one enabled cooling codex row + fallback_claude -> both True; claude_free={'claude:sonnet': 2, 'claude:opus': 0} -> executors['claude:sonnet']['free'] == 2, ['claude:opus']['free'] == 0, claude_free_total == min(2, claude_workers_free), with Pool.claude_has_headroom and Pool.pick patched to raise; claude_free=None -> Claude rows report max_parallel - running; Claude-only pool all cooling -> capacity._reason 'cooldown' with fallback False.\n\nIf a test exposes a defect in the implementation, fix it in the three source files (in scope) and say so in the result. Do not rename or weaken existing tests. The task branch is behind goal/T-1403 by the B4a commits (gitutil.py); do not touch gitutil.py or tests/test_gitutil.py; the merge rebase brings them in.\n\nCommit first, then run tests/test_executor.py tests/test_pool.py tests/test_capacity.py in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate.",
